eld at home and he's  ticked off and you look at this  offensive line these young guys played  outstanding you know they played  outstanding you know and if you protect  patrick mahomes with that run game and  with travis kelsey tyreek hill  and let me just say this joe woods did a  terrible job of defending tyreke hill  you can't treat him like he's an  ordinary wide receiver he's not he's one  of the top two or three wide receivers  in all of football you have to double  team this guy there's no reason by one  cornerback i don't think there's one  quarterback in the national football  league that can defend this guy the  entire game you have to double team you  have to switch up play some man play  some zone jam him off the line of  scrimmage he is so fast and so dynamic  what sense does it make if you play  eight yards off of him but you never  touch him when he comes off the line of  scrimmage i just never understood this  philosophy then you have travis kelsey  who's athletic so when they play the  baltimore ravens this week what does  marlon humphrey do does he double team  um ty does he cover tyrek hill does he  cover travis kelsey that's going to be a  problem so they have to figure out what  they're going to do with their best  cornerback and how he could defend two  guys because there's nobody else that  could defend tyree kill or travis kelsey  and it's about every time tyreek hill  catches the ball it doesn't really  matter where he gets a catch it just  feels like it turns into a punt return  you know what i mean he kind of catches  it he stops looks around for a second  sort of evaluates where the defenders  are and then he's so lethal after the  catch being able to just pick what he  wants to do and where he wants to go he  sometimes he picks up 10 sometimes 20.  sometimes he breaks it for an 80 yard  touchdown and then the other one is when  mahomes starts gaining time back there  when he starts just buying extra time  back there behind the offensive